# Normalize line endings in the repository, not in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (set in the *system* gitconfig on Windows,
# outside this repo) rewrites every tracked text file to CRLF on checkout and
# back to LF on commit. The Biome formatter expects LF, so a fresh Windows
# checkout reports the entire tree as mis-formatted.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes Git store LF in the object database AND check out LF
# on every platform, so the working tree matches the blobs and the formatter
# gate is deterministic for contributors and for CI on any runner OS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.exe binary
*.db binary
*.db-wal binary
*.db-shm binary